  "id": "exponential-curve",
  "term": "exponential curve",
  "definition": "An exponential curve is a mathematical pattern used to describe how a measure changes over time, such as model error as more data become available. In this context, an asymptotic exponential curve is used to track whether results are approaching a stable level or equilibrium.",
